<title>MEXICO: Mexico's vehicle output rises in first four months.</title>
<headline>Mexico's vehicle output rises in first four months.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's automobile industry produced 414,328 vehicles in the first four months of the year, compared with 396,381 during the same period in 1996, the Mexican Automobile Industry Association (AMIA) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Mexico also exported 307,799 vehicles from January through April, 1997 against 321,313 in the year-ago period, the AMIA said.  </p>
<p>The following table compares production and sales data for cars and trucks and buses during the relevant periods.</p>
<p>				   JAN-APRIL 97	    JAN-APRIL 96</p>
<p>    TOTAL PRODUCTION	     414,328		  396,381</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 100,518		   71,131</p>
<p>		autos		   72,376			n/a</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    28,142			n/a</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   313,810		  325,250</p>
<p>TOTAL SALES</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC MARKET	 125,662		   94,185</p>
<p>	   EXPORT MARKET	   307,799		  321,313</p>
<p>		autos		  187,182		  215,266</p>
<p>		trucks and buses   120,617		  106,047</p>
<p>	   DOMESTIC RETAIL SALES 122,547		   87,726</p>
<p>		autos		   76,995			n/a</p>
<p>		trucks and buses    45,552			n/a</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
